Z||000000||william_thorniii||10-11-2000||12:56 PM||||Friends,<P>I am considering the GM parts bin performance upgrade to my braking system.  Does anyone know pertinent information regarding F and Y body spindle diameters, bolt patterns etc.  Basically, I would like to mount y-body disks, calipers, rotors, bearings and hubs to my new DROP spindles.  <P>Is there any information out there?  I have tried to do research on this topic myself, but have had no luck finding information on braking/susp components on either of the aforementioned cars.  If anyone knows of any site out there, your help is greatly appreciated.  Otherwise all you F/Y body gearheads out there... it is a time to test your knowledge.  <P>Many Thanks,<P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>85 GT (for sale)<BR>86 SE (project car)<BR>87 EC (driver)||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfixit58||10-11-2000||01:09 PM||||WT,<P>New DROP spinldes? Weren't you just commenting on how hard they are to find? Or, were the lucky individual who got the last pair from Carparts.com?<P>Regarding spindle diameters: when ever I need info like that I head over to my local U-pull-it yard and take along my measuring tape. If no one has the info your looking for, perhaps this option will work for you.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||10-11-2000||02:23 PM||||mrfix18,<P>Yes I have been looking for spindles for quite some time.  Missed out on the carparts.com order though.  I placed an order for two sets and 3 days later received a cancellation notice since they were out of stock.  I found an alternate source.  The check goes out today.  I should have them by the middle of next week.  <P>Good suggestion about the bone yard.  I have had a difficult time finding Y-bodies in the bone yard though.  You are right with the F-bodies, even 4th gen are dime a dozen there.  <P>William T. Thorn, III  ||||reg||1
