Z||000005||william_thorniii||10-11-2000||04:11 PM||||Carrolles,<P>I didn't word that properly.  It really isn't a new supplier.  It is that Street Dreams now has 7 pairs (6 excluding mine) that will be finished early next week.  They told me that they were going to give those that have contacted them in the past first dibs.  I imagine that what it will really boil down to is who gets them the money first.  The new price (ignore the one on their site) is $349 + S&H.  The good news is that for all of you running stock wheels.. they fit even with the 15's.  <P>For those of you that do not know how to contact Street Dreams... here goes...<P>Street Dreams<BR>4833 Cherry Valley Road<BR>Middleville, MI 49333<BR>616.795.3100<BR>strdream@iserv.net<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||007DOUG||10-11-2000||11:04 PM||||HOLY CRAP, $349. My ebay drop spindles were a good deal.  <P>I do not have street dream spindles, I have bell tech's, BUT 15" rims would NOT fit with my spindles. I had to go with 16"<P>The rim rubs on the tierod during a turn. I hope SD solved this. <P>||||reg||1
